      "human_review_status": "no independent human review documented by the seed",
      "independent_reproduction_status": "none documented by the seed",
      "latex": "\\begin{gathered}r,s\\ge1,\\qquad \\Phi_{r,s}(A,B)=(AB,\\operatorname{Res}(A,B)),\\\\\\det D\\Phi_{r,s}=(-1)^{s(r+1)}(r-s)\\operatorname{Res}(A,B)^2.\\\\r\\ne s\\Longrightarrow \\widetilde X_{r,s,\\ell}\\longrightarrow U_{r,s,\\ell}\\text{ is a finite \\acute{e}tale }\\mu_{|s-r|}\\text{-torsor},\\\\\\deg(\\widetilde X_{r,s,\\ell}\\to\\{C\\in V_{r+s}:\\ell(C)=1\\})=|s-r|\\binom{r+s}{r},\\\\\\mathcal R_{r,s},\\mathcal S_{r,s,\\ell}\\text{ prime}\\Longrightarrow\\operatorname{Cl}(U_{r,s,\\ell})\\simeq\\mathbb Z/|s-r|\\mathbb Z.\\end{gathered}",
      "natural": "Let r,s>=1 and choose the standard monomial coefficient orders on V_r, V_s, and V_{r+s}. For Phi_{r,s}(A,B)=(AB,Res(A,B)), det D Phi_{r,s}=(-1)^{s(r+1)}(r-s)Res(A,B)^2. In particular, if r!=s, Phi_{r,s} is etale on the coprime locus {Res!=0}. For nonzero ell in V_{r+s}^*, if r!=s, projectivisation is a finite etale mu_{|s-r|}-torsor from the normalized slice tilde X_{r,s,ell} to U_{r,s,ell}; the induced multiplication map has generic degree |s-r| binom(r+s,r); and, if the resultant divisor R_{r,s} and multiplication-hyperplane divisor S_{r,s,ell} are prime, Cl(U_{r,s,ell}) is isomorphic to Z/|s-r|Z.",
